#!/bin/sh
# xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland custom_picker_binary. The running burl shell
# shows the chooser and writes XDPH's "[SELECTION]..." reply into a FIFO;
# without a reachable shell this falls back to the stock picker.

set -u

token=false
for arg; do
    [ "$arg" = --allow-token ] && token=true
done

dir=$(mktemp -d "${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/burl-share-picker.XXXXXX") || exit 1
trap 'rm -rf "$dir"' EXIT
trap 'exit 1' INT TERM
mkfifo "$dir/reply" || exit 1

# qs ipc exits 0 even when the target is missing, so look for pick's answer.
ack=$(burl-shell ipc --any-display call sharepicker pick \
    "$dir/reply" "$token" "${XDPH_WINDOW_SHARING_LIST:-}" 2>/dev/null)
if [ "$ack" != ready ]; then
    rm -rf "$dir"
    exec hyprland-share-picker "$@"
fi

# A share request nobody answers would hold XDPH's portal call open.
if ! timeout 300 cat "$dir/reply"; then
    burl-shell ipc --any-display call sharepicker cancel >/dev/null 2>&1
fi
